<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:49:16Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>How AI worsens online violence against Middle East women</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d3b1dc963ad312a7d6148c595ded2bcea9722bb2e11ec4ed17c9be49bd129c82</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:48:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T06:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-ai-worsens-online-violence-against-middle-east-women/a-79912634--666dfdf1ad89.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-ai-worsens-online-violence-against-middle-east-women/a-79912634?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Women in the Middle East already have to deal with an above-average share of online harassment and violence. The proliferation of AI-enabled tools is making it worse.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>British counterterrorism police arrest US soldier accused of spying on behalf of Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:201d78cff0a003fda6adb5aa9c1ba7ef63e0049676db652be365ec0e9fa2b5e7</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:49:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T19:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/british-counterterrorism-police-arrest-us-soldier-accused-of-spying-on-behalf-of-russia/a-79913240--5991e0a904a3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/british-counterterrorism-police-arrest-us-soldier-accused-of-spying-on-behalf-of-russia/a-79913240?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A member of the US Army has been arrested near Gloucester in England. Police said he was suspected of espionage activity in connection with Russia. Investigators from the US and UK are involved in the probe.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UK Privy Council overrules Trinidad and Tobago gay sex law</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6c3070b40fb1c77d5e918e57cb196a56c48f7a77a19f04174c814cae8c03d010</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:49:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T19:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-privy-council-overrules-trinidad-and-tobago-gay-sex-law/a-79912163--f186aba38925.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-privy-council-overrules-trinidad-and-tobago-gay-sex-law/a-79912163?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A London court has overturned a Trinidad and Tobago law criminalizing consensual sexual relations between male same-sex couples. As a result of the colonial legacy, it is the independent country's last court of appeal.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Victims of Nazi war in Poland call on Germany for support</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6ab7102b3e66a8efa4b6c71ade068b5c1fa7b1add47fc213fc682bb31a12eb3a</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:49:16Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T17:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/victims-of-nazi-war-in-poland-call-on-germany-for-support/a-79909311--36756d6320e4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/victims-of-nazi-war-in-poland-call-on-germany-for-support/a-79909311?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">More than 80 years after the end of World War II, Polish victims of the Nazi regime are still waiting for a "humanitarian gesture" from Germany. The 2027 draft budget hasn't left them much hope for possible reparations.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran denies role in fridge hack, France summons ambassador</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c4753290b3cb7af181761e974b62ea1447f879ff98d21700fc9afac96f020c64</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:47:57Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T15:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-denies-role-in-fridge-hack-france-summons-ambassador/a-79910206--6d0355211a72.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-denies-role-in-fridge-hack-france-summons-ambassador/a-79910206?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">France has said it rules "nothing" out in response to a cyberattack on supermarket refrigeration units. Iran, however, said it categorically rejected Paris' "baseless and one-sided accusations" of IRGC involvement.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Controversial kinship: From colonial rule to the Holocaust?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:21163ec83bab351c4c0ef7cb74ac42d0c94e9ce1241dbfc9e4131aa24587fd06</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:47:57Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T15:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/controversial-kinship-from-colonial-rule-to-the-holocaust/a-79902228--16129c6452e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/controversial-kinship-from-colonial-rule-to-the-holocaust/a-79902228?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hitler once called Eastern Europe "Germany's India." A new exhibition examines the links between colonialism and Nazism, and the bitter debate over where comparisons illuminate history and where they fall short.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Japan watches for signs of change in Trump's foreign policy priorities</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd6d0b4dafd2049c69af3984909bcbbc661d307258eb48a76b26c0b1373eeffb</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:47:57Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T13:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/japan-watches-for-signs-of-change-in-trump-s-foreign-policy-priorities/a-79909398--c0dcb3ef3493.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/japan-watches-for-signs-of-change-in-trump-s-foreign-policy-priorities/a-79909398?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Tokyo fears the drubbing US President Donald Trump suffered in last week's midterm election may push him to pursue a diplomatic quick win at the expense of Washington's allies in the Indo-Pacific.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Bulgaria highway pileup kills 12, dozens injured: PM</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a65b8fd3940adee300d1e7f3e32f61f1cbb94f1f58d86d628a4c299747bf5d36</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:47:57Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T11:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-highway-pileup-kills-12-dozens-injured-pm/a-79907978--e4c51329b4c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-highway-pileup-kills-12-dozens-injured-pm/a-79907978?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At least 12 people were killed and dozens injured in a series of crashes caused by thick fog in Bulgaria. Police, firefighters and paramedics were dispatched to the scene for the rescue operation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Online disinformation rife after Krakow mass shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b8d38551d7b24e6698ee0bcce54938ea1e1b14a9c9496f9c5bdd1e004dbbe4ca</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:47:57Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T10:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-online-disinformation-rife-after-krakow-mass-shooting/a-79900620--80ad1afffb68.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-online-disinformation-rife-after-krakow-mass-shooting/a-79900620?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fake and AI-manipulated images spread online in the hours after the Krakow attack, fueling false narratives about the mass shooting. DW Fact Check examined what's real, and what isn't.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>New trilateral talks on Ukraine war in Abu Dhabi: What to expect?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4e07c09e564cbf7f6058da0d90c53a00c65146ae01f98c39955685817d926ecb</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:47:57Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T23:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/new-trilateral-talks-on-ukraine-war-in-abu-dhabi-what-to-expect/a-79905734--3c6da76b72e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/new-trilateral-talks-on-ukraine-war-in-abu-dhabi-what-to-expect/a-79905734?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian and Russian representatives last met in February for talks on ending the war, but the same sticking points remain. Ukraine continues to demand security guarantees, which is a non-starter for Russia.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Russia: Independent Novaya Gazeta shuts its Moscow newsroom</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:52860c8a55795b97b8ccafafea4aeae1632c41faaf2cd6771157d6156fe96ecd</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:47:57Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T16:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-independent-novaya-gazeta-shuts-its-moscow-newsroom/a-79899827--d187f3fbc3fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-independent-novaya-gazeta-shuts-its-moscow-newsroom/a-79899827?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The investigative newspaper is closing its doors after Russian authorities labeled it a "foreign agent" and ordered it vacate its Moscow premises.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India's demonetization: 10 years on, economic benefits still disputed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cceae6405d0589c85f532d71bd1eaa2b8e056ef51106469c08f8aee06df3e015</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:47:57Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T16:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-s-demonetization-10-years-on-economic-benefits-still-disputed/a-79903331--2fc450e61f09.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-s-demonetization-10-years-on-economic-benefits-still-disputed/a-79903331?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A decade after the 2016 currency ban, its impact on India's economy and the fight against black money remains contested.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
